{"availability":"available","full":"yairEO/color-picker","name":"color-picker","description":"Minimal javascript color picker component","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":78,"forks":5,"created":"2020-12-09T17:49:03Z","updated":"2025-05-23T05:29:31Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://yaireo.github.io/color-picker","topics":["color","color-picker","colorpicker","component","javascript","javascript-component","ui","vanilajs","widget"],"demo":"https://yaireo.github.io/color-picker","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T07:20:44.932Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T07:20:44.932Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T07:20:44.932Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T20:15:07.009Z","stars":78,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-09T23:07:54.057Z","stars":78,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-13T07:36:58.127Z","stars":78,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-19T07:20:44.932Z","stars":78,"forks":5}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This color-picker component is based on my previous work with highly customizable range input (slider) component: UI-Range and the power of HSLA color format infused into custom CSS properties (variables) to allow as lightweight solution as possible.","I have hand-crafted the color transformation functions to be as lightweight as possible, and kept the UI to the minimum necessary to provide the user with a better, unified, color-picking experience which I believe is better than the default which looks different across browsers and OS, and does not allow modifications to a color's alpha (opacity) channel.","Since this component is only a color-picker, and does not transforms or interacts with any elements on the page, it is up to developers, if they wish, to connect it to an input and have the color-picker positioned next to it in a popup-manner. Such behavior can be seen seen in the demo page and below, on the last section."],"features":["Carefully crafted as lightweight as possib